  "releaseNotes": "[9.0.0] - 2026-08-10\n      - .NET10 support, optimizations (includes breaking API changes)\n      [8.4.1] - 2026-08-02\n      - Interceptor fixes\n      [8.4.0] - 2026-07-31\n      - Added support for CancellationToken to default repository\n      - Moved extensions to parent namespace for ease of use\n      - Added query extensions\n      [8.3.2] - 2026-06-16\n      - Fixed parameter duplication on query retry\n      [8.3.1] - 2026-05-18\n      - Reworked exception handling in transactions and queries due to errors in transiency\n      [8.3.0] - 2026-05-13\n      - Added support for CancellationToken to SQL queries\n      - Improved transient error handling in transactions\n      - Improved transient error handling in queries\n      - SaveChanges now uses result objects\n      [8.2.0] - 2026-04-19\n      - Added error handling for transaction rollbacks\n      [8.1.2] - 2026-02-09\n      - Added overloads for InTransaction and InTransactionAsync for return by value\n      [8.1.1] - 2026-02-12\n      - Added additional converters for datetime types\n      - Added extensions for autoresolved query ordering\n      - Fixed query ordering in default repository\n      [8.1.0] - 2026-01-11\n      - TransactionContext now isolated per DatabaseFacade\n      - UnitOfWork is now disposable\n      - UnitOfWork now creates its own DbContext instance by using the provided factory\n      - UnitOfWork no longer implements Attach/Detach methods\n      - Repositories now implement Attach/Detach methods\n      - GenericRepository renamed to DefaultRepository\n      - Sql queries now contain SqlFirstOrDefaultAsync/RawSqlFirstOrDefaultAsync methods\n      - Sql queries now return IReadOnlyList instead of array to improve performance (less reallocations)",
